 cardiac cells: its biochemical and pharmacological properties and its role in regulating internal concentrations of sodium and internal pH.</article-title><source>J Mol Cell Cardiol</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>1029</fpage><lpage>1042</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3001319</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005422-Bier1"><label>5</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bier</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Bodmer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title><italic>Drosophila</italic>, an emerging model for cardiac disease.</article-title><source>Gene</source><volume>342</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15527959</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005422-Wolf1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolf</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Amrein</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Izatt</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Choima</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Reedy</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title><italic>Drosophila</italic> as a model for the identification of genes causing adult human heart disease.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><volume>103</volume><fpage>1394</fpage><lpage>1399</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16432241</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005422-Haddad1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haddad</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Enhancing our understanding of the molecular responses to hypoxia in mammals using <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic>.</article-title><source>J Appl Phy